--[[
	ORE ICONS. Generated by tools/gen-ore-icons.js -- do not hand-edit.

	512x512 uploaded art, one icon and one case per ore, keyed by ORE ID (not
	by name: names get retyped, ids are load-bearing in the datastore).

	Why uploaded assets rather than MineOreArt's packed-pixel pipeline: that one
	rebuilds 64x64 faces at runtime via EditableImage, which is right for
	procedural block faces. These are 512x512 authored art -- 43 million pixels
	across 164 images -- so packing them would be hundreds of megabytes of Luau.
	Uploaded images are CDN-served and cost nothing at runtime.

	82 ores x 2 = 164 assets.

	THE `icon` IDS ARE THE 2026-10-06 RENDERS. Owner: "only use the ores i just
	gave u, and use the cases for the rare drops". The earlier icons were flat
	vector art; these are rendered 3D objects in the same style as the tool
	skins, supplied as one Canva SVG sheet and cut out by
	tools/icons/svg-icon-extract.js.

	The sheet held 84 icons for 82 ores and the two spares were INSIDE the run,
	not appended: by tier 51 the order had already slipped by one. Colour
	matching could not identify them -- both candidates it proposed were
	plausible ores -- so the owner named them, a plain speckled ingot at icon-20
	and a teal runed ingot at icon-76. Skipping those two lines the rest up, and
	the landmarks confirm it: tier 69 Frostfire is the fire-and-ice cluster, 72
	Orichalcum the runed bronze ingot, 73 Spectrite the prismatic crystal, 74
	Mythril the luminous blue ingot.

	`case` is untouched and still the ore-case art, which is what rare drops use.
]]

